3. INTEGRATED MATHEMATICAL FORMULAS\
The ECU unit calculates the system state using the following precise formulas:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Phi = ABS( (V_gps * K_abs) - (Omega_axleB * R_dynamic) )
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 
\f2\i The target value for engagement is Phi < 0.02. V_gps is the true vehicle speed, K_abs is the road surface friction coefficient, Omega_axleB is the angular velocity of the Sigma axle, and R_dynamic is the dynamic rolling radius of the tire.
\f0\i0 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
R_dynamic = R_nominal * (1 - (Load_coeff * Pressure_psi))
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 
\f2\i This accounts for tire deformation based on load and air pressure.
\f0\i0 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
T_regen = (0.5 * J * Omega^2) / Delta_t
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 
\f2\i This determines the regenerative braking intensity based on axle moment of inertia (J), angular velocity (Omega), and braking time (Delta_t).
\f0\i0 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
T_total = T_active(t) + T_standby(t) = Constant
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 
\f2\i This ensures that traction is not interrupted during the axle swap.
\f0\i0 \
